{{also|Thwaite}}
==English==

===Etymology 1===
From {{inh|en|enm|*thwait}}, a borrowing from {{der|en|non|þveit|t=paddock}}. Compare Old Norse {{m|non|þveita|t=to hurl}} (see {{m|en|whittle}}), Danish {{m|da|døjt}} (“1/160 of the gulden”, dialectal: “a small coin”), German {{m|de|Deut}}, Dutch {{m|nl|duit}}. Cognate with {{cog|ang|þwītan|t=to thwite; cut; cut off}}. {{doublet|doit|lang=en}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|/θweɪt/|lang=en}}

====Noun====
{{en-noun}}

# {{lb|en|archaic}} A piece of [[forest]] [[land]] [[cleared]] for [[agriculture]] or [[habitation]]; a [[clearing]]; [[assart]]

